    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1280">

                <pb facs="0880" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/22.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Miller to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-11-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 19, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Cándido Aguilar to-day sent communication to Huasteca Petroleum Company
                    placing company war tax at $100,000. Complete copy this second demand being
                    forwarded by mail. As yet have received no answer to letter sent to General
                    Aguilar but copy issued was read to-day over telephone to his representative at
                    Juan Casiano when he presented these second demands.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Miller</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
